{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_sync_strategy", "label": "SYNC-STRATEGY.md \u2014 Mobile/Web Sync Model", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/SYNC-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_sync_strategy_cache_then_network", "label": "Cache-then-Network Sync Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/SYNC-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Paint disposable local cache instantly, throttled (30 s) network refresh, in-memory listener sets for cross-screen freshness; Supabase Postgres is the single source of truth and web never fetches more eagerly than mobile."}, {"id": "docs_sync_strategy_no_realtime", "label": "No-Realtime Decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/SYNC-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Realtime would require adding tables to the supabase_realtime publication (a backend change affecting both clients) while mobile doesn't consume it \u2014 the apps could still diverge; refresh-on-focus polling matches mobile exactly."}, {"id": "docs_sync_strategy_no_mutation_queue", "label": "No Offline Mutation Queue", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/SYNC-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74-5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The queue was removed from mobile and client_sync_id's unique index deliberately dropped; all writes online-only on both clients, and web must NOT add one \u2014 it would break parity; concurrent edits are last-write-wins per whole-row UPDATE."}, {"id": "docs_sync_strategy_fx_snapshots", "label": "Snapshot-Computed Historical Views", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/SYNC-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captu